{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And he shall draw near (ונגש)</b> — three times in the Masorah, and the others: \"and the priest shall draw near (ונגש הכהן)\"; \"the plowman shall draw near (ונגש חורש) to the reaper.\" Just as Moses drew near alone, so the priest enters alone into the Holy of Holies to pray there for the year that it be proper, as written: \"the plowman shall draw near (ונגש חורש) to the reaper.\"" "<b>They shall draw near (יגשו)</b> — two times: \"but they shall not draw near (והם לא יגשו),\" \"they shall draw near one by one (אחד באחד יגשו).\" Meaning: each and every one enters further inside than his fellow, as they said: Moses — a partition for himself, etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The juxtaposition reads across three occurrences of ונגש: Exodus 24:2, Amos 9:13, and one cited as ונגש הכהן (Joel 2:17 or Amos 7:14 depending on reading)."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:16.975567093Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}